---
title: What Happens in One Step (One k-means Iteration)
---
flowchart TD
    Start(["User clicks Step"]) --> A

    A["1. ASSIGN<br/>Every sticker measures its distance<br/>to every current panel centre"]
    A --> ATie{"Exact tie?<br/>(within 1e-12)"}
    ATie -- Yes --> ATieResolve["Earlier centre wins<br/>(source order)"]
    ATie -- No --> AWin["Closest centre wins"]
    ATieResolve --> B
    AWin --> B

    B["2. UPDATE<br/>Each centre moves to the average<br/>position of its assigned stickers"]
    B --> BEmpty{"Any panel empty?"}
    BEmpty -- Yes --> BKeep["That centre stays exactly<br/>where it was (no divide by zero)"]
    BEmpty -- No --> BMove["Centre moves to the new average"]
    BKeep --> C
    BMove --> C

    C["3. MEASURE<br/>Add up every sticker's squared<br/>distance to its NEW centre<br/>(this is the Total Squared Error)"]
    C --> D

    D["4. CHECK<br/>Did every sticker land on the<br/>SAME centre as last iteration?"]
    D -- "No -- something changed" --> E["Status: RUNNING<br/>Ready for another Step"]
    D -- "Yes -- nothing changed" --> F["Status: CONVERGED<br/>Step and Run to End both stop here"]
    D -- "Still changing after 20 tries" --> G["Status: NOT_CONVERGED<br/>(safety stop, keeps last state visible)"]

    F --> H(["Save Final Wall button turns on"])
